229
00:15:44,631 --> 00:15:45,671
Ogi.

230
00:15:46,111 --> 00:15:47,511
Now come go!

231
00:15:59,671 --> 00:16:00,871
Five-sword!

232
00:16:02,871 --> 00:16:04,911
Three-thousand worlds!

233
00:16:10,311 --> 00:16:19,671
Sometimes strange and unexplained things happen here on the Grand Line.

234
00:16:21,071 --> 00:16:26,271
Things like sailors being fine one minute, then suddenly losing their memories during a voyage.

235
00:16:26,911 --> 00:16:29,311
I'm sure you've both heard stories like that before.

236
00:16:29,611 --> 00:16:32,631
You think that same sort of phenomenon is happening on this island?

237
00:16:32,631 --> 00:16:40,271
On that stone monument we passed on the way here, there was a story inscribed about a monster who lives off of people's memories.

238
00:16:41,171 --> 00:16:43,411
It's said it's made this island its home.

239
00:16:44,091 --> 00:16:48,331
It's practically a legend, but that is the explanation that seems to make the most sense.

240
00:16:48,331 --> 00:16:56,511
Since new memories are created every day, this creature must be consuming the memories of the people of this island little by little.

241
00:16:56,751 --> 00:16:59,531
I see. So it's kind of like raising a broiler.

242
00:17:01,771 --> 00:17:04,051
I'm having a hard time buying that story.

243
00:17:04,511 --> 00:17:07,071
